& [Purpose]
  + define the smallest runnable one-shot process boundary over published semantic inspection wire without authorizing any broader host service provider model or effect surface

& [SJSProcessing]
  + delineation selects only no-argument invocation bounded stdin admission exact wire dispatch exclusive stdout-or-host-fault publication and fixed exit disposition
  + semantic refinement defines host as one process one complete request one complete response or one bounded public fault rather than a resident service transport session or shell
  + constraint reapplication preserves exact wire bytes nested semantic refusal response sealing replay non-authority and every predecessor bound
  + pruning removes paths filesystem sockets network configuration environment clocks threads authentication MCP LSP provider model update remote and persistence concerns
  + seven-fold exhaustion finds no smaller executable seam than a one-shot EOF-bounded stdio adapter over the closed wire function
  + data-driven design makes arguments stdin count stdout count stderr fault class bytes-written state exit disposition and zero non-stdio effects the complete host data plane

& [Requirements]
  + [CSIH-001] replay the exact four-file published source snapshot at28799 bytes and preserve the protected live C state
  + [CSIH-002] add one safe-Rust executable target named cantor-sop-inspect-stdio under the published wire component
  + [CSIH-003] accept exactly zero command arguments and expose no argument-controlled operation path or output destination
  + [CSIH-004] read stdin with a fixed-size buffer and stop at MAX_WIRE_REQUEST_BYTES plus one without allocating or retaining additional input
  + [CSIH-005] require one nonempty byte sequence and observed EOF before outer parsing validation or semantic dispatch
  + [CSIH-006] refuse read failure empty input or overflow before calling cantor_sop_inspect_wire respond
  + [CSIH-007] dispatch admitted input only through cantor_sop_inspect_wire respond with no semantic translation fallback or second attempt
  + [CSIH-008] write a successful returned wire response byte-for-byte to stdout with no prefix suffix newline encoding or normalization
  + [CSIH-009] complete stdout with write_all and flush before returning the successful exit disposition
  + [CSIH-010] transport a governed nested semantic refusal as its exact sealed wire response and successful host exit rather than a host fault
  + [CSIH-011] map argument input outer-wire and pre-output publication faults to one fixed bounded public stderr code and one fixed nonzero exit disposition
  + [CSIH-012] never include request bytes paths nested values raw OS diagnostics or library error text in public stderr
  + [CSIH-013] emit either one complete stdout response or one public stderr fault and never claim both
  + [CSIH-014] after any stdout byte is attempted emit no alternate stderr payload or second response and use only nonzero exit if completion fails
  + [CSIH-015] perform no semantic dispatch more than once and no read write or flush after the terminal disposition is fixed
  + [CSIH-016] keep public stderr within128 ASCII bytes and stdout within MAX_WIRE_RESPONSE_BYTES
  + [CSIH-017] preserve deterministic stdout bytes and exit disposition for identical admitted stdin across fresh processes
  + [CSIH-018] expose no filesystem path database cache socket network listener service thread clock random environment shell provider model operator update remote mutation or publication API
  + [CSIH-019] make stdin read stdout write optional bounded stderr write and process exit the complete new authority surface
  + [CSIH-020] cover constructive success empty page pagination and nested semantic refusal in fresh-process debug and overflow-checked release tests
  + [CSIH-021] cover argument empty malformed duplicate unknown trailing oversized incomplete read broken output and response-bound adversaries without echo or unauthorized dispatch
  + [CSIH-022] statically prove dependency and source absence for filesystem network service environment shell provider model and mutation surfaces
  + [CSIH-023] pass exact workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format dual-host source formation retained evidence and script parsing gates
  + [CSIH-024] attribute publish and immediately bookend only after completion signature direct remote equality and bounded-effect replay

& [AcceptanceGates]
  + [CSIH-A01] one valid request through a fresh process produces the exact direct wire response bytes and successful exit
  + [CSIH-A02] every pre-dispatch host fault is fixed bounded non-echoing and proves zero semantic dispatch
  + [CSIH-A03] stdout publication is atomic in claim: completion is success and any partial or failed completion is only nonzero exit with no alternate payload
  + [CSIH-A04] static focused and complete workspace evidence agree that only governed stdio and exit effects exist
  + [CSIH-A05] publication records exact implementation and immediate bookend commits without merge service provider model remote or non-stdio effect authority

& [Excluded]
  + command options paths files SQLite cache index sockets network HTTP MCP LSP resident service sessions authentication concurrency environment configuration provider model inference shell child process installation update remote machine product effect and merge

& [Status]
  + formed_for_exact_bounded_implementation_only
